We install the Conversation registry item from your engine’s tree. Select the tab for your engine, copy the complete command, and run it at your project root. When the CLI finishes, you should see the paths it wrote, starting with components/ai/conversation.tsx.
nativewinduniwindnpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/nativewind/conversation.jsonCopynpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/uniwind/conversation.jsonCopy

We install the Message registry item. The conversation item does not install it automatically, and the message list needs it. You should see components/ai/message.tsx among the paths the CLI reports, along with the peers both items declare.
nativewinduniwindnpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/nativewind/message.jsonCopynpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/uniwind/message.jsonCopy

We install the composed PromptInput together with the Item and Sheet registry items its installed source imports. You should see components/ai/prompt-input.tsx, components/ui/item.tsx, and components/ui/sheet.tsx written into your project by one command.
nativewinduniwindnpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/nativewind/prompt-input.json https://rnraielements.com/r/nativewind/item.json https://rnraielements.com/r/nativewind/sheet.jsonCopynpx @react-native-reusables/cli@latest add https://rnraielements.com/r/uniwind/prompt-input.json https://rnraielements.com/r/uniwind/item.json https://rnraielements.com/r/uniwind/sheet.jsonCopy

We add the seed transcript at shared/quickstart-messages.ts. The file is identical for both engines, so pick either panel and copy the complete source. You should see 24 authored turns in the file, from Seed turn 01: Plan a weekend walk. to Seed turn 24: Ready for your message.
